1
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:14,000
Two strangers fell in love. One knew it wasn't by chance.

2
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Bounce is a drama, romance film directed by Don Roos.

3
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:30,000
Buddy Amaral, a successful and self-absorbed Los Angeles advertising executive, switches airline tickets with a stranger just
before boarding a long-delayed flight so that he might enjoy an overnight fling with a pretty Dallas businesswoman.

4
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:38,000
When the plane goes down, killing all aboard, Buddy's
guilt soon turns into an alcohol problem.

5
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:46,000
As part of his 12-step program, Buddy seeks atonement and decides
to seek out the woman he thinks he's left a widow.

6
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:54,000
Buddy Amaral, played by Ben Affleck.

7
00:49:56,000 --> 00:50:02,000
Abby Janello, played by Gwyneth Paltrow.

8
00:57:04,000 --> 00:57:10,000
Mimi Prager, played by Natasha Henstridge.

9
01:04:12,000 --> 01:04:18,000
Greg Janello, played by Tony Goldwyn.

10
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:26,000
Seth, played by Johnny Galecki.

11
01:18:28,000 --> 01:18:34,000
Jim Willer, played by Joe Morton.

12
01:25:36,000 --> 01:25:42,000
Bounce is a 2000 American romantic drama film directed by Don
Roos, and starring Ben Affleck and Gwyneth Paltrow.

13
01:32:44,000 --> 01:32:50,000
The film explores themes of stroke of fate, chance,
loss of loved one, widow, alcoholism.

14
01:39:52,000 --> 01:39:58,000
The tone is emotional.
